formal-conjectures
------------------
The problem statements and the definitions they use come from formal-conjectures
(https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures, commit
9097e2f90e66d2f6244209cb1c07f7120d17ec53), Copyright 2025 and 2026 The Formal Conjectures Authors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. They are adapted (with the original copyright lines and
a statement of the changes) in palomar/*/Challenge.lean and palomar/*/*/Defs.lean. Four short lemmas
copied from the same files (lebesgueFunction_eq, μ_sum_eq_one, μFamily_univ, localTime_le_maxLocalTime)
are marked in the files that contain them.

Material by another Left to Solve participant (not licensed by this repository)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
palomar/mo-10799-weak-kahn-kalai/ contains about 75 lines (the definitions mu, M, I and the lemmas sd1,
sd2, sd3, mu_nonneg, mu_ins0, mu_ins1, M_insert, I_insert in namespace OMA10799W) from Left to Solve
PR #341 by the GitHub user Genbox. Left to Solve has no licence file, and no licence for these lines has
been granted.

Hadamard sequence data
----------------------
The sequence data in palomar/hadamard-first-cases/ were regenerated from published tables: the numbers
were extracted from the tables compiled in SageMath (https://www.sagemath.org, GPL-2.0-or-later) and
re-encoded as Lean data. No SageMath code is included. The papers the numbers come from are cited in
the proof file.

scripts/check-lean-sources.py follows PalomarRegistry/PalomarTemplate's script of the same name
(Apache-2.0).
